        <h2>Best Wide-Seat Chairs for Tall Users: By Use Case</h2>

        <h3>Best for tall users 6'3"+ who are also broad-shouldered: Steelcase Leap Plus</h3>
        <p>The Leap Plus (~21" seat width) is the only mainstream ergonomic chair that combines a genuinely wide seat with the seat height ceiling (22.5") and adjustable depth (17"–19.75") required for users above 6'3". At 500 lb weight capacity, it also handles larger frames structurally.</p>
        <p>The ~21" seat width is not the absolute maximum in the market, but it is wide enough for virtually all hip widths in practice — and it comes with the dimensional and ergonomic capabilities that other wide-seat chairs sacrifice. The La-Z-Boy Trafford is technically wider (~22") but caps seat height at ~21" and has a fixed seat depth, making it inappropriate for users above 6'2" as a primary ergonomic solution.</p>
        <p>Full analysis: <a href="/review/leap-plus/" class="link-internal">Steelcase Leap Plus review →</a></p>

