        <h3>Best for tall users 6'0"–6'3" who run warm: Herman Miller Aeron Size C</h3>
        <p>The Aeron Size C (~20.5" seat width) provides a wide seat alongside the Pellicle mesh construction (mesh seat and back) that gives the Aeron its heat-management advantage. For tall, broad-shouldered users who prioritize breathability, the Size C is the strongest option in this range.</p>
        <p>Constraint: fixed ~18.5" seat depth is adequate through 6'2" but not for users with longer-than-average femurs. And the 350 lb weight capacity is the lowest in this comparison — not a big-and-tall option for heavier users. For breadth-and-cooling-focused users in the 6'0"–6'3" range with a standard or light frame, the Aeron C earns its recommendation.</p>
        <p>Full analysis: <a href="/review/aeron-size-c/" class="link-internal">Herman Miller Aeron Size C review →</a></p>

